class Solution(object):
    def isPalindrome(self, x):
        return str(x) == str(x)[::-1]


Here 'x' is given as number, but we type-cast it to string using 'str(x)'.
'str(x)' returns same number but as string data-type.
'str(x)[::-1]' returns the reversed 'x'

For E.x.:
x = 123
str(x) = "123"
str(x)[::-1]  = "321"
Compare, if they are equal then palindrome otherwise not.
